: protocol: OpenAI Chat Completions, streaming; HTTP 200, then an error object arrives as a data payload, then the stream ends
: provenance: CONSTRUCTED by R2. The OpenAI API reference does NOT document a mid-stream error payload for Chat Completions
:   (checked 2026-11-11). The shape used here — a data line whose JSON has a top-level "error" object with
:   message/type/param/code — is inferred from:
:   - the official Python SDK, which raises APIError when an SSE data payload "is_mapping(data) and data.get("error")"
:     (https://raw.githubusercontent.com/openai/openai-python/main/src/openai/_streaming.py, checked 2026-11-11)
:   - the documented non-stream error fields error.code / error.type / error.param
:     (https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/error-codes, checked 2026-11-11)
: other servers differ: OpenRouter documents an "error" object on choices with code/message/metadata and normalises
:   finish_reason to "error" (https://openrouter.ai/docs/api/reference/overview); Ollama's docs do not specify.
: note: no [DONE] and no usage chunk follow. Treat EOF without [DONE] and without finish_reason as a disconnect.
: note: the partial tool call (index 0) never completes. It MUST NOT produce ToolCallReady.
: expected ModelEvents: TextDelta("Let me check"), Failed(kind=server_error, retryable=true, partial_output_emitted=true). Usage unknown.

